1
00:01:38,984 --> 00:01:42,000
[Episode 24]

2
00:01:42,799 --> 00:01:43,799
Hello, Uncle Sun.

3
00:01:43,799 --> 00:01:45,040
Happy New Year.

4
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:47,680
<i>Ye. Happy New Year.</i>

5
00:01:47,680 --> 00:01:50,070
- I wanted to...
- <i>Wait a moment.</i>

6
00:01:50,070 --> 00:01:51,280
Okay.

7
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:53,560
<i>Number 101, please.
Window three for your medicine.</i>

8
00:01:53,560 --> 00:01:55,496
<i>That's me. Thank you.</i>

9
00:01:55,496 --> 00:01:57,680
<i>Ye, go ahead.</i>

10
00:01:57,680 --> 00:01:59,200
Wait, Uncle Sun, what's wrong?

11
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:01,046
Why are you at the hospital?

12
00:02:01,046 --> 00:02:02,519
<i>I'm fine.</i>

13
00:02:02,519 --> 00:02:04,519
<i>My mother-in-law just had an operation.</i>

14
00:02:04,519 --> 00:02:05,879
<i>I'm picking up her medicine.</i>

15
00:02:05,879 --> 00:02:07,319
<i>I've got good news for you, Ye.</i>

16
00:02:07,319 --> 00:02:09,599
<i>There's been an update on your dad's case.</i>

17
00:02:09,599 --> 00:02:11,879
<i>But I can't go into details right now.</i>

18
00:02:11,879 --> 00:02:13,080
<i>So,</i>

19
00:02:13,080 --> 00:02:14,838
<i>what did you need me for?</i>

20
00:02:14,838 --> 00:02:16,400
Nothing, it's fine now.

21
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:18,480
Just sending my New Year's greetings.

22
00:02:19,439 --> 00:02:21,439
I'll let you go.

23
00:02:21,439 --> 00:02:23,600
Let's catch up later.

24
00:02:31,960 --> 00:02:34,560
I'll handle the money.

25
00:02:34,560 --> 00:02:36,360
Don't worry about it.

26
00:02:42,919 --> 00:02:45,680
Hey, Ye, come over.

27
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:47,680
Coming!

28
00:02:58,803 --> 00:03:01,160
Auntie. What is it?

29
00:03:06,719 --> 00:03:09,000
I just went to Xuan Island to pack some things.

30
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:10,520
And I found these.

31
00:03:10,520 --> 00:03:12,080
They still work fine.

32
00:03:12,080 --> 00:03:14,159
I'm going to start doing quick cuts.

33
00:03:14,159 --> 00:03:15,854
Five yuan a haircut.

34
00:03:15,854 --> 00:03:17,659
Quick cuts?

35
00:03:18,522 --> 00:03:20,785
I'll go to parks or the dock

36
00:03:20,785 --> 00:03:21,960
and give haircuts.

37
00:03:21,960 --> 00:03:24,080
It's fast and cheap.

38
00:03:24,080 --> 00:03:25,240
That should make quite a bit

39
00:03:25,240 --> 00:03:26,898
to cover daily living costs.

40
00:03:26,898 --> 00:03:27,920
Auntie,

41
00:03:27,920 --> 00:03:29,439
you really have great business sense.

42
00:03:29,439 --> 00:03:31,344
- Seriously?
- Yes.

43
00:03:34,319 --> 00:03:35,719
People always need haircuts.

44
00:03:35,719 --> 00:03:37,120
Get out there

45
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:39,719
and you might get more customers.

46
00:03:39,719 --> 00:03:40,960
I'll go and help you out.

47
00:03:40,960 --> 00:03:43,640
- Just stay home and study hard.
- Just stay home and study hard.

48
00:03:45,520 --> 00:03:48,000
But I want to help too.

49
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,080
Grandma needs someone to be with her.

50
00:03:50,080 --> 00:03:52,200
Being with her is helping too.

51
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:54,639
Okay, then it's settled.

52
00:03:54,639 --> 00:03:56,439
Alright, I hope everything goes well.

53
00:03:56,439 --> 00:03:57,960
Good luck.

54
00:04:03,319 --> 00:04:05,840
- Money! Money! Money!
- Money! Money! Money!

55
00:04:12,353 --> 00:04:14,353
I'm coming in, Ye.

56
00:04:14,353 --> 00:04:15,639
Auntie.

57
00:04:15,639 --> 00:04:17,560
You're still up?

58
00:04:17,560 --> 00:04:18,759
Well...

59
00:04:18,759 --> 00:04:22,000
I-I wanted to ask you to do me a favor.

60
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:24,480
- Sit down. What is it?
- Okay.

61
00:04:25,198 --> 00:04:27,240
I'm starting my stall tomorrow

62
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:29,680
and I need a sign.

63
00:04:29,680 --> 00:04:31,040
But my handwriting is awful.

64
00:04:31,040 --> 00:04:32,715
I've tried several times, but it looks awful.

65
00:04:32,715 --> 00:04:35,519
You have nice handwriting. Can you help me?

66
00:04:35,519 --> 00:04:37,099
I'll do it for you.

67
00:04:42,120 --> 00:04:43,840
Let's do it like this.

68
00:05:00,565 --> 00:05:03,098
[Quick Cut]
[Five Yuan Each]

69
00:05:03,959 --> 00:05:05,959
What do you think, Auntie? Look.

70
00:05:05,959 --> 00:05:08,199
It's perfect, Ye!

71
00:05:08,199 --> 00:05:09,360
You did it so fast,

72
00:05:09,360 --> 00:05:11,120
just like that.

73
00:05:11,120 --> 00:05:13,439
It looks like it was printed at a store.

74
00:05:13,439 --> 00:05:14,600
You're exaggerating.

75
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:16,240
I just wrote a few simple words, Auntie.

76
00:05:16,240 --> 00:05:18,640
But it's really nice.

77
00:05:19,278 --> 00:05:20,560
By the way, Auntie,

78
00:05:20,560 --> 00:05:22,759
it's so tough for you out there.

79
00:05:22,759 --> 00:05:25,079
Take my gloves and hat.

80
00:05:25,079 --> 00:05:27,797
It's freezing, you have to wear them.

81
00:05:28,553 --> 00:05:29,680
Don't forget to wear them

82
00:05:29,680 --> 00:05:31,896
while you're doing haircuts.

83
00:05:31,896 --> 00:05:32,920
Or you'll freeze.

84
00:05:32,920 --> 00:05:34,399
We got this hat together

85
00:05:34,399 --> 00:05:36,399
last time at the market.

86
00:05:36,399 --> 00:05:38,000
Put this on too. It'll keep your ears warm.

87
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:40,079
Ye, you're so thoughtful.

88
00:05:40,079 --> 00:05:41,360
But let me tell you,

89
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:42,839
as long as I'm

90
00:05:42,839 --> 00:05:45,160
thinking about money,

91
00:05:45,160 --> 00:05:47,120
I get so pumped

92
00:05:47,120 --> 00:05:48,806
and don't feel the cold.

93
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:50,500
Look.

94
00:05:50,500 --> 00:05:53,199
Don't you think the character
for "Cut" is very interesting?

95
00:05:53,199 --> 00:05:55,160
The top part is "Qian," meaning early.

96
00:05:55,160 --> 00:05:56,879
The bottom part is "Dao," meaning suffering.

97
00:05:56,879 --> 00:05:59,079
So, do you think that...

98
00:05:59,079 --> 00:06:00,879
if we go through suffering

99
00:06:00,879 --> 00:06:03,319
in our early years,

100
00:06:03,319 --> 00:06:05,680
we'll be able to enjoy happiness later?

101
00:06:05,680 --> 00:06:08,199
So this character means that, doesn't it?

102
00:06:08,199 --> 00:06:10,079
I think...

103
00:06:10,079 --> 00:06:11,959
you're right.

104
00:06:11,959 --> 00:06:14,360
We'll definitely enjoy happiness later.

105
00:06:14,360 --> 00:06:15,600
Exactly.

106
00:06:15,600 --> 00:06:16,600
I just don't believe

107
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:18,439
that I'm destined to be unlucky forever.

108
00:06:18,439 --> 00:06:21,399
There's a saying, what was it?

109
00:06:21,399 --> 00:06:24,519
Something like "...comes a rainbow"? Or...

110
00:06:24,519 --> 00:06:26,399
After every storm comes a rainbow.

111
00:06:26,399 --> 00:06:28,680
Yes, it's coming!

112
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:29,959
Money is coming!

113
00:06:29,959 --> 00:06:32,003
Coming.

114
00:06:32,003 --> 00:06:33,399
Ye.

115
00:06:33,399 --> 00:06:36,279
I haven't taken good care of you before.

116
00:06:36,279 --> 00:06:38,720
I'll work twice as hard

117
00:06:38,720 --> 00:06:40,943
to take good care of you.

118
00:06:40,943 --> 00:06:42,531
Auntie,

119
00:06:42,531 --> 00:06:43,571
I'm already living

120
00:06:43,571 --> 00:06:46,120
a very good life.

121
00:06:46,120 --> 00:06:49,120
As long as our family stays together,

122
00:06:49,120 --> 00:06:50,920
that's happiness.

123
00:06:55,079 --> 00:06:57,347
My dear, sweet Ye.

124
00:07:20,799 --> 00:07:22,279
Alright, everyone, stop writing.

125
00:07:22,279 --> 00:07:24,033
Time's up.

126
00:07:24,033 --> 00:07:27,120
I'm sending the answers to the group chat now.
Check your answers.

127
00:07:27,120 --> 00:07:28,551
<i>Put the questions you got wrong in the group.</i>

128
00:07:28,551 --> 00:07:30,959
<i>We'll go over them together this afternoon.</i>

129
00:07:30,959 --> 00:07:32,240
<i>Math first,</i>

130
00:07:32,240 --> 00:07:33,600
then Physics, Chemistry, and Biology.

131
00:07:33,600 --> 00:07:35,320
In that order.

132
00:07:44,040 --> 00:07:46,000
Why are you giving me red packets?

133
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:47,759
<i>I did well on the finals last semester.</i>

134
00:07:47,759 --> 00:07:50,000
<i>So for New Year's,
my dad gave me a big red packet.</i>

135
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:51,519
<i>It's all thanks to you.</i>

136
00:07:51,519 --> 00:07:54,199
<i>So you deserve a share too.</i>

137
00:07:54,199 --> 00:07:55,879
<i>I was at my grandparents' house.</i>

138
00:07:55,879 --> 00:07:58,600
<i>I had nowhere to use my New Year's money,</i>

139
00:07:58,600 --> 00:08:00,240
<i>so I'll use it for tutoring.</i>

140
00:08:00,240 --> 00:08:02,399
<i>I didn't give you that for tutoring.</i>

141
00:08:02,399 --> 00:08:04,040
<i>You're my cousin.</i>

142
00:08:04,040 --> 00:08:06,360
<i>A brother should give his sister a red packet.</i>

143
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:07,759
<i>Just take it.</i>

144
00:08:07,759 --> 00:08:09,560
<i>Qing Ye, if you're given a red packet here,</i>

145
00:08:09,560 --> 00:08:10,561
<i>you have to take it.</i>

146
00:08:10,561 --> 00:08:11,606
<i>If you don't,</i>

147
00:08:11,606 --> 00:08:13,399
<i>it's like rejecting good fortune.</i>

148
00:08:13,399 --> 00:08:15,079
I know.

149
00:08:15,079 --> 00:08:17,400
You're all just trying to help me.

150
00:08:20,197 --> 00:08:22,802
The excuses you've all come up with...

151
00:08:24,120 --> 00:08:26,399
are just too good to refuse.

152
00:08:26,399 --> 00:08:28,720
It's really hard for me to say no.

153
00:08:28,720 --> 00:08:30,959
Then I'll just accept them.

154
00:08:30,959 --> 00:08:33,040
Thank you all for your kindness.

155
00:08:34,679 --> 00:08:35,759
<i>Qing Ye,</i>

156
00:08:35,759 --> 00:08:37,600
<i>what has Wu been up to lately?</i>

157
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:39,119
<i>We haven't seen him around.</i>

158
00:08:39,119 --> 00:08:42,600
<i>Is he still coming to our study sessions?</i>

159
00:08:42,600 --> 00:08:44,679
<i>Is he coming back to class?</i>

160
00:08:44,679 --> 00:08:46,720
Don't worry, everyone.

161
00:08:47,399 --> 00:08:49,840
I'll make sure he doesn't slack off.

162
00:09:09,561 --> 00:09:11,181
<i>I've sent today's study notes</i>

163
00:09:11,181 --> 00:09:12,360
<i>to you on WeChat.</i>

164
00:09:12,360 --> 00:09:14,399
<i>You can take a look after work.</i>

165
00:09:14,399 --> 00:09:16,360
<i>Ask me anytime if you're confused.</i>

166
00:09:16,360 --> 00:09:18,000
Wu, happy New Year.

167
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:19,080
Happy New Year.

168
00:09:19,080 --> 00:09:20,399
You came so early.

169
00:09:20,399 --> 00:09:21,603
If you're not proactive at work,

170
00:09:21,603 --> 00:09:23,440
there's a problem with your attitude.

171
00:09:24,285 --> 00:09:25,966
Here's your start-of-work red packet.

172
00:09:27,519 --> 00:09:29,519
- No need.
- Just take it.

173
00:09:29,519 --> 00:09:30,639
It's from my sister.

174
00:09:30,639 --> 00:09:33,440
Consider it an advance on your salary.

175
00:09:33,440 --> 00:09:34,519
That's even worse.

176
00:09:34,519 --> 00:09:36,200
No pay before work.

177
00:09:36,200 --> 00:09:37,240
We're so close.

178
00:09:37,240 --> 00:09:38,519
Now or later, it's the same.

179
00:09:38,519 --> 00:09:40,039
- Take it.
- It's different.

180
00:09:40,039 --> 00:09:41,919
What if I work too much this month

181
00:09:41,919 --> 00:09:44,211
and you and Shu Han end up paying me less?

182
00:09:45,458 --> 00:09:47,519
Then I'll make it up to you.

183
00:09:47,519 --> 00:09:48,519
How about this?

184
00:09:48,519 --> 00:09:49,560
Daily pay,

185
00:09:49,560 --> 00:09:51,448
cash in hand.

186
00:09:51,448 --> 00:09:53,560
That's easier for everyone.

187
00:09:55,279 --> 00:09:56,279
Alright then.

188
00:09:56,279 --> 00:09:57,399
Later,

189
00:09:57,399 --> 00:09:59,320
I'll tell my sister about it.

190
00:10:00,465 --> 00:10:02,266
Wu, happy New Year.

191
00:10:02,266 --> 00:10:03,272
Happy New Year.

192
00:10:03,272 --> 00:10:05,960
I've got a phone here.
Can you take a look at it?

193
00:10:05,960 --> 00:10:07,759
Why do you have another phone to fix?

194
00:10:07,759 --> 00:10:08,960
It's my grandma's.

195
00:10:08,960 --> 00:10:12,279
She wants to watch dramas every day,
but the screen won't stop flashing.

196
00:10:12,279 --> 00:10:13,920
Let me see.

197
00:10:16,399 --> 00:10:18,039
Wu, it's not much.

198
00:10:18,039 --> 00:10:20,080
Just a little something from the guys.

199
00:10:21,720 --> 00:10:22,960
Wait,

200
00:10:22,960 --> 00:10:24,460
are you treating me like a lucky cat?

201
00:10:24,460 --> 00:10:26,399
Everyone's lining up to hand me money.

202
00:10:26,399 --> 00:10:28,759
We all know that you're short on cash now.

203
00:10:28,759 --> 00:10:30,920
We just want to help you out.

204
00:10:32,287 --> 00:10:33,486
Forget the money.

205
00:10:33,486 --> 00:10:34,720
If you really want to help,

206
00:10:34,720 --> 00:10:36,279
just find me more jobs.

207
00:10:36,279 --> 00:10:37,920
Daily pay, cash in hand, if possible.

208
00:10:37,920 --> 00:10:39,000
No problem.

209
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:40,240
I've already told everyone.

210
00:10:40,240 --> 00:10:41,519
There will be plenty of work.

211
00:10:41,519 --> 00:10:44,552
If you can't find other jobs,
come here and help me fix some motorcycles.

212
00:10:44,552 --> 00:10:46,200
I'm short-staffed too.

213
00:10:46,200 --> 00:10:47,600
Sure.

214
00:10:47,600 --> 00:10:49,558
Thanks.

215
00:10:49,558 --> 00:10:51,160
Good luck with the opening.

216
00:10:51,799 --> 00:10:53,120
Bye, Wu.

217
00:10:53,120 --> 00:10:55,480
- I'll call you when it's fixed.
- Okay.

218
00:11:02,600 --> 00:11:05,080
<i>I realize that the past cannot be recalled,</i>

219
00:11:05,080 --> 00:11:08,120
<i>but the future is still within reach.</i>

220
00:11:08,120 --> 00:11:10,639
<i>I'm not that far off from the right track.</i>

221
00:11:10,639 --> 00:11:13,799
<i>Yesterday I was lost, but today I see the path.</i>

222
00:11:13,799 --> 00:11:16,160
<i>Lightly floats and drifts the boat.</i>

223
00:11:17,039 --> 00:11:19,360
Insist.

224
00:11:19,360 --> 00:11:22,000
Insist on doing something.

225
00:11:24,120 --> 00:11:25,200
<i>You have a new order.</i>

226
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:27,240
<i>Please accept it.</i>

227
00:11:57,012 --> 00:11:58,039
Sir.

228
00:11:58,039 --> 00:12:00,680
Take a look. Is this okay?

229
00:12:01,639 --> 00:12:04,039
It's good and fast. Very efficient.

230
00:12:04,039 --> 00:12:05,159
Thank you.

231
00:12:05,159 --> 00:12:06,200
From now on,

232
00:12:06,200 --> 00:12:08,000
please recommend me to more people.

233
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:10,120
- No problem.
- I'm here every day.

234
00:12:10,120 --> 00:12:11,361
Just scan the code up there.

235
00:12:11,361 --> 00:12:13,279
- Okay.
- Next, please.

236
00:12:13,279 --> 00:12:15,039
- I've already paid.
- Okay, thank you.

237
00:12:15,039 --> 00:12:17,120
Have a seat.

238
00:12:17,120 --> 00:12:18,720
Do you want to keep it long

239
00:12:18,720 --> 00:12:20,039
or go short?

240
00:12:20,039 --> 00:12:21,080
You decide.

241
00:12:21,080 --> 00:12:22,760
Alright.

242
00:12:26,999 --> 00:12:28,919
Sir! Wait a moment!

243
00:12:28,919 --> 00:12:30,760
Sir!

244
00:12:32,120 --> 00:12:33,679
Sir!

245
00:12:33,679 --> 00:12:35,960
Sir!

246
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:37,039
Please wait!

247
00:12:37,039 --> 00:12:38,279
Sir!

248
00:12:38,279 --> 00:12:39,639
Sir!

249
00:12:39,639 --> 00:12:41,400
Wait a second, sir!

250
00:12:41,400 --> 00:12:42,799
Sir!

251
00:12:42,799 --> 00:12:44,399
Sir!

252
00:12:44,399 --> 00:12:46,040
Sir!

253
00:12:48,440 --> 00:12:50,759
Who are you?

254
00:12:50,759 --> 00:12:52,653
Sir, please.

255
00:12:52,653 --> 00:12:54,560
I didn't get the payment.

256
00:12:55,639 --> 00:12:57,600
I-I thought it went through.

257
00:12:57,600 --> 00:12:59,760
Maybe the signal was bad.

258
00:13:01,279 --> 00:13:03,000
- It's gone through now.
- I've received it.

259
00:13:03,639 --> 00:13:05,800
Don't let it happen again.

260
00:13:09,625 --> 00:13:10,840
Mr. Zhu,

261
00:13:10,840 --> 00:13:11,879
thank you.

262
00:13:11,879 --> 00:13:13,519
- Don't mention it.
- What's up?

263
00:13:13,519 --> 00:13:15,120
- I...
- Let me give you a haircut.

264
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:17,520
- Okay. Let's go.
- Okay.

265
00:13:30,333 --> 00:13:32,200
This physics question...

266
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:07,639
I fell asleep.

267
00:14:07,639 --> 00:14:09,800
What did you say?

268
00:14:13,519 --> 00:14:14,919
I can't believe you actually got

269
00:14:14,919 --> 00:14:16,320
this tough physics problem right.

270
00:14:16,320 --> 00:14:17,920
Let me see.

271
00:14:19,879 --> 00:14:21,520
Is it that difficult?

272
00:14:33,519 --> 00:14:34,600
Up until now,

273
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:38,120
only Ye Ying Jian and I got it right.

274
00:14:38,120 --> 00:14:40,600
It requires some spatial imagination.

275
00:14:42,960 --> 00:14:44,879
I don't rely on imagination.

276
00:14:44,879 --> 00:14:46,360
I rely on manual labor.

277
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:49,080
I need to get to work soon.

278
00:14:49,080 --> 00:14:52,053
Are you coming home tonight?

279
00:14:52,053 --> 00:14:54,440
You haven't been home in nearly a week.

280
00:14:54,440 --> 00:14:57,399
Ye Ying Jian's uncle
set up an electronics factory.

281
00:14:57,399 --> 00:14:58,960
It'll be open after the Lantern Festival.

282
00:14:58,960 --> 00:15:00,368
I need to install security cameras early.

283
00:15:00,368 --> 00:15:03,080
And the control panel on Fuzz's uncle's boat

284
00:15:03,080 --> 00:15:04,440
broke again.

285
00:15:04,440 --> 00:15:05,799
Anyway, lately...

286
00:15:05,799 --> 00:15:08,320
if there's work, I'll take it.

287
00:15:49,360 --> 00:15:51,907
Look at you, a woman out here
in the bitter cold with a stall.

288
00:15:51,907 --> 00:15:53,759
Five bucks and he still rips you off?

289
00:15:53,759 --> 00:15:55,080
What a jerk.

290
00:15:55,080 --> 00:15:56,840
That's business.

291
00:15:56,840 --> 00:15:58,160
I've seen plenty of those people.

292
00:15:58,160 --> 00:16:00,159
- I'm used to it.
- That's not right.

293
00:16:00,159 --> 00:16:01,560
Lu Xun once said,

294
00:16:01,560 --> 00:16:04,520
"Is it right just because it's always been so?"

295
00:16:06,159 --> 00:16:07,960
Mr. Zhu,

296
00:16:07,960 --> 00:16:09,920
I might not fully get

297
00:16:09,920 --> 00:16:12,159
what you just said,

298
00:16:12,159 --> 00:16:14,200
but it sounds right to me.

299
00:16:14,200 --> 00:16:16,000
You're absolutely right.

300
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:17,120
As for me,

301
00:16:17,120 --> 00:16:18,519
I really need to thank you.

302
00:16:18,519 --> 00:16:19,525
What for?

303
00:16:19,525 --> 00:16:22,279
I remember last time you went with me

304
00:16:22,279 --> 00:16:24,399
to plead with your ex-wife, Xiao Lian.

305
00:16:24,399 --> 00:16:27,000
And this time, for just five yuan,

306
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:28,120
you helped me get it back.

307
00:16:28,120 --> 00:16:30,360
- No, no...
- Shouldn't I thank you for all that?

308
00:16:30,360 --> 00:16:32,400
Forget about last time.

309
00:16:32,400 --> 00:16:34,200
But this time, it was just right.

310
00:16:34,200 --> 00:16:35,759
I mean, you earned that money

311
00:16:35,759 --> 00:16:37,399
through your hard work.

312
00:16:37,399 --> 00:16:39,320
Five yuan is still money, isn't it?

313
00:16:39,320 --> 00:16:40,679
I really enjoy talking to

314
00:16:40,679 --> 00:16:42,440
educated people like you.

315
00:16:42,440 --> 00:16:45,560
It really makes me feel so much better.

316
00:16:45,560 --> 00:16:48,080
Our Ye is the same way, you know.

317
00:16:48,080 --> 00:16:49,720
She just says a few words,

318
00:16:49,720 --> 00:16:51,278
and suddenly everything makes sense to me.

319
00:16:51,278 --> 00:16:52,879
- It's great to be educated.
- Doesn't it...

320
00:16:52,879 --> 00:16:54,919
give you a feeling of sudden enlightenment?

321
00:16:54,919 --> 00:16:57,760
- Right?
- Yes, yes, enlightenment.

322
00:16:57,760 --> 00:16:59,320
By the way, Lan Fang,

323
00:16:59,320 --> 00:17:01,440
what about Xing Wu and Qing Ye?

324
00:17:02,440 --> 00:17:04,359
Turn back around.

325
00:17:04,359 --> 00:17:05,683
I'm still cutting. Don't move,

326
00:17:05,683 --> 00:17:07,920
or I'll mess it up.

327
00:17:07,920 --> 00:17:10,079
I'm just saying,

328
00:17:10,079 --> 00:17:11,200
well...

329
00:17:11,200 --> 00:17:13,406
in Xing Wu and Qing Ye's situation,

330
00:17:13,406 --> 00:17:15,920
they could get some financial aid
once the new semester begins.

331
00:17:15,920 --> 00:17:17,320
The government now has

332
00:17:17,320 --> 00:17:18,680
special policies for children

333
00:17:18,680 --> 00:17:20,799
from families with financial difficulties.

334
00:17:20,799 --> 00:17:21,920
Let's not go back

335
00:17:21,920 --> 00:17:23,359
to how it was before.

336
00:17:23,359 --> 00:17:25,600
Don't let them suddenly drop out again.

337
00:17:28,039 --> 00:17:30,200
So, you're afraid...

338
00:17:33,238 --> 00:17:34,960
I won't let Wu go to school

339
00:17:34,960 --> 00:17:36,480
and you're here to convince me today?

340
00:17:36,480 --> 00:17:37,640
No.

341
00:17:37,640 --> 00:17:39,079
I mainly just

342
00:17:39,079 --> 00:17:41,759
wanted to come and get a haircut.

343
00:17:41,759 --> 00:17:43,062
Don't worry.

344
00:17:43,062 --> 00:17:45,119
I won't.

345
00:17:45,119 --> 00:17:47,279
This time, even if Wu doesn't want to,

346
00:17:47,279 --> 00:17:48,720
I'll drag him there myself

347
00:17:48,720 --> 00:17:50,039
to make sure he goes to school

348
00:17:50,039 --> 00:17:51,200
and takes his exams.

349
00:17:51,200 --> 00:17:52,701
Just don't worry.

350
00:17:52,701 --> 00:17:53,839
Lan Fang,

351
00:17:53,839 --> 00:17:56,079
you've become different.

352
00:17:56,079 --> 00:17:58,446
- Different? Really?
- Yes.

353
00:18:00,412 --> 00:18:02,240
Do I look older?

354
00:18:02,240 --> 00:18:03,319
No, you...

355
00:18:03,319 --> 00:18:05,560
You've become more open-minded.

356
00:18:08,264 --> 00:18:10,318
Okay. There you go.

357
00:18:10,318 --> 00:18:12,519
I look much sharper after the cut.

358
00:18:12,519 --> 00:18:13,640
Forget about the money.

359
00:18:13,640 --> 00:18:15,279
You've got a coupon, right?

360
00:18:15,279 --> 00:18:17,319
I lost that coupon ages ago.

361
00:18:17,319 --> 00:18:18,799
I'll accept it anyway.

362
00:18:18,799 --> 00:18:20,160
We're good.

363
00:18:20,160 --> 00:18:21,519
<i>50 yuan received.</i>

364
00:18:21,519 --> 00:18:23,720
Mr. Zhu, that's too much.

365
00:18:23,720 --> 00:18:25,640
It's for next time. I'm off, Lan Fang.

366
00:18:25,640 --> 00:18:27,280
Thank you!

367
00:18:27,960 --> 00:18:30,640
You've got nine more left. Don't forget.

368
00:18:39,079 --> 00:18:40,561
Coming!

369
00:18:40,561 --> 00:18:43,120
I'm coming!

370
00:18:46,411 --> 00:18:48,200
It smells so good, Auntie.

371
00:18:48,200 --> 00:18:50,680
What did you make?

372
00:18:50,680 --> 00:18:52,359
Qing Ye, you're back!

373
00:18:52,359 --> 00:18:53,519
Perfect timing.

374
00:18:53,519 --> 00:18:55,160
Come on, let's eat.

375
00:18:55,160 --> 00:18:56,720
Hurry.

376
00:18:58,104 --> 00:18:59,115
Come on.

377
00:18:59,115 --> 00:19:00,359
Grandma.

378
00:19:00,359 --> 00:19:01,839
Ye, you're back.

379
00:19:01,839 --> 00:19:04,640
Come, come. Let's eat.

380
00:19:04,640 --> 00:19:08,320
Auntie, did you have a good day today?

381
00:19:09,400 --> 00:19:10,759
30?

382
00:19:10,759 --> 00:19:13,079
30 customers! Pretty good, right?

383
00:19:13,079 --> 00:19:14,600
That's amazing!

384
00:19:14,600 --> 00:19:16,326
No wonder we're having braised pork trotters.

385
00:19:16,326 --> 00:19:17,880
Let me smell.

386
00:19:18,639 --> 00:19:19,759
It smells delicious!

387
00:19:19,759 --> 00:19:22,079
Auntie, you've hit the jackpot!

388
00:19:22,079 --> 00:19:23,839
Grandma gave me the money.

389
00:19:23,839 --> 00:19:25,440
She told me to cook something good for you.

390
00:19:25,440 --> 00:19:27,440
Ye, you eat first.

391
00:19:27,440 --> 00:19:29,160
Here, Grandma. Let me get you some.

392
00:19:29,160 --> 00:19:31,359
You eat first. A big one for you.

393
00:19:31,359 --> 00:19:32,400
Okay, okay.

394
00:19:32,400 --> 00:19:34,880
- Here.
- Thank you.

395
00:19:34,880 --> 00:19:37,039
So, Lan Fang, just listen to me.

396
00:19:37,039 --> 00:19:39,880
- You've got to spend this money.
- That's right.

397
00:19:39,880 --> 00:19:42,079
Don't skimp on the children's food.

398
00:19:42,079 --> 00:19:43,160
Yes.

399
00:19:43,160 --> 00:19:45,319
Too bad Wu isn't here today.

400
00:19:45,319 --> 00:19:47,280
He's gonna miss this.

401
00:19:48,160 --> 00:19:49,799
It's okay, Grandma.

402
00:19:49,799 --> 00:19:51,680
I'll bring some to him.

403
00:19:52,519 --> 00:19:54,800
Good, here.

404
00:20:06,920 --> 00:20:08,759
Wu, someone's here for you.

405
00:20:08,759 --> 00:20:10,280
Okay.

406
00:20:12,064 --> 00:20:13,465
Why did you come?

407
00:20:13,465 --> 00:20:15,905
Auntie had a good day. She made pork trotters.

408
00:20:15,905 --> 00:20:17,039
I was afraid you'd miss out,

409
00:20:17,039 --> 00:20:19,120
so I brought some for you.

410
00:20:20,920 --> 00:20:22,599
It's still hot.

411
00:20:22,599 --> 00:20:24,371
Auntie knows you're hauling goods,

412
00:20:24,371 --> 00:20:25,840
and she's afraid your hands will crack.

413
00:20:25,840 --> 00:20:27,760
So she bought you some hand cream.

414
00:20:29,279 --> 00:20:30,960
Grandma worried you'd get too cold,

415
00:20:30,960 --> 00:20:33,480
so she made you a pair of gloves.

416
00:20:35,400 --> 00:20:36,920
Take them.

417
00:20:38,160 --> 00:20:39,640
What about you?

418
00:20:39,640 --> 00:20:42,000
Did you bring me something too?

419
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:43,960
Of course I've got a gift for you.

420
00:20:43,960 --> 00:20:45,240
And my gift

421
00:20:45,240 --> 00:20:47,160
will definitely clear your mind

422
00:20:47,160 --> 00:20:48,759
and sharpen your senses.

423
00:20:48,759 --> 00:20:51,000
Don't tell me it's that...

424
00:20:52,038 --> 00:20:53,720
It's exactly what you think.

425
00:20:53,720 --> 00:20:55,120
Look.

426
00:20:55,839 --> 00:20:58,040
My handwritten problem set.

427
00:20:58,040 --> 00:20:59,160
What's so funny?

428
00:20:59,160 --> 00:21:01,560
These are the most important parts. The best!

429
00:21:01,560 --> 00:21:03,640
I want you to go over it carefully

430
00:21:03,640 --> 00:21:06,320
in your spare time to relax.

431
00:21:07,512 --> 00:21:08,559
Since you're here

432
00:21:08,559 --> 00:21:10,400
and even brought me such a precious gift,

433
00:21:10,400 --> 00:21:12,079
I'll take you to a great place.

434
00:21:12,079 --> 00:21:13,640
Where?

435
00:21:13,640 --> 00:21:16,279
A great place for a luxury buffet.

436
00:21:16,279 --> 00:21:18,400
But we already have braised pork trotters.

437
00:21:18,400 --> 00:21:20,319
This is an extra treat for you.

438
00:21:20,319 --> 00:21:21,839
Given our current situation,

439
00:21:21,839 --> 00:21:23,190
buffets cost way too much.

440
00:21:23,190 --> 00:21:24,703
And now, is there any buffet still open?

441
00:21:24,703 --> 00:21:27,200
Come on. You'll see when we get there.

442
00:21:28,559 --> 00:21:29,960
Let's go.

443
00:21:37,180 --> 00:21:38,760
Here we are.

444
00:21:39,879 --> 00:21:42,279
This is your idea of a luxury buffet?

445
00:21:42,279 --> 00:21:43,334
Ten yuan each.

446
00:21:43,334 --> 00:21:45,200
Lots of options, eat as much as you like.

447
00:21:45,200 --> 00:21:47,440
Ten yuan? That's so cheap.

448
00:21:47,440 --> 00:21:49,680
And it's unlimited?

449
00:21:49,680 --> 00:21:50,920
Really?

450
00:21:50,920 --> 00:21:52,320
Okay, sweet and sour pork...

451
00:21:52,320 --> 00:21:54,379
- Fried fish.
- Fried fish and Mapo Tofu!

452
00:21:54,379 --> 00:21:57,520
Then what are we waiting for? Let's dig in!

453
00:21:58,159 --> 00:21:59,737
I'm starving.

454
00:21:59,737 --> 00:22:00,759
I'm so hungry.

455
00:22:00,759 --> 00:22:01,920
I took one sniff.

456
00:22:01,920 --> 00:22:04,240
This fried fish smells amazing.

457
00:22:04,240 --> 00:22:05,680
Here.

458
00:22:09,892 --> 00:22:11,080
It's delicious.

459
00:22:11,080 --> 00:22:13,440
The bones are all crispy.

460
00:22:15,135 --> 00:22:17,240
This is good too.

461
00:22:17,240 --> 00:22:21,240
Don't forget the pork trotter soup
Auntie made for you.

462
00:22:21,240 --> 00:22:22,640
Have some too.

463
00:22:22,640 --> 00:22:23,965
No, I already had some.

464
00:22:23,965 --> 00:22:25,680
I'm afraid you'll choke.

465
00:22:36,738 --> 00:22:37,970
Xing Wu.

466
00:22:38,612 --> 00:22:39,640
Zhang.

467
00:22:39,640 --> 00:22:41,680
Your girlfriend?

468
00:22:41,680 --> 00:22:43,449
- She's my sister.
- He's my brother.

469
00:22:43,449 --> 00:22:44,559
So pretty.

470
00:22:44,559 --> 00:22:46,119
You're so lucky.

471
00:22:46,119 --> 00:22:47,400
Enjoy your meal.

472
00:22:47,400 --> 00:22:48,880
Bye.

473
00:22:52,173 --> 00:22:54,120
Just a guy I worked with this morning.

474
00:22:58,960 --> 00:23:00,320
Don't choke.

475
00:23:00,320 --> 00:23:01,800
I won't.

476
00:23:01,800 --> 00:23:03,800
I'm not a kid.

477
00:23:10,600 --> 00:23:12,640
You know what,

478
00:23:12,640 --> 00:23:15,185
today I absolutely had

479
00:23:15,185 --> 00:23:18,039
a brand new life experience.

480
00:23:18,039 --> 00:23:19,153
What was it?

481
00:23:19,153 --> 00:23:21,400
The feeling of a pauper getting rich.

482
00:23:21,400 --> 00:23:23,668
So much good food for only ten yuan.

483
00:23:23,668 --> 00:23:25,759
I'm so full.

484
00:23:25,759 --> 00:23:27,240
Slow down, slow down.

485
00:23:27,240 --> 00:23:29,000
I'm so full I can barely walk.

486
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:30,216
At this rate,

487
00:23:30,216 --> 00:23:31,920
we'll miss the last bus.

488
00:23:31,920 --> 00:23:33,452
Then what do we do?

489
00:23:34,211 --> 00:23:36,519
- I'll carry you on my back.
- No way, I couldn't do that.

490
00:23:36,519 --> 00:23:37,960
My stomach is so stuffed,

491
00:23:37,960 --> 00:23:40,240
I'll throw up if it gets pressed.

492
00:23:40,240 --> 00:23:41,840
Okay, okay.

493
00:23:43,805 --> 00:23:45,840
What are you laughing at?

494
00:23:46,519 --> 00:23:47,839
I just remembered,

495
00:23:47,839 --> 00:23:49,640
half a year ago,

496
00:23:49,640 --> 00:23:51,040
who was it that said...

497
00:23:51,040 --> 00:23:53,319
"1,000 yuan a week for meals.

498
00:23:53,319 --> 00:23:56,160
Refund the leftover, pay the extra." Who?

499
00:23:56,160 --> 00:23:57,720
Me. It was me.

500
00:23:57,720 --> 00:23:59,079
Happy now?

501
00:23:59,079 --> 00:24:00,960
To be honest, I really regret

502
00:24:00,960 --> 00:24:02,880
blowing money like that back then.

503
00:24:02,880 --> 00:24:04,200
That 1,000 yuan,

504
00:24:04,200 --> 00:24:05,672
if I had saved it until now,

505
00:24:05,672 --> 00:24:08,160
I could've eaten a hundred meals here.

506
00:24:08,160 --> 00:24:09,559
It's okay.

507
00:24:09,559 --> 00:24:11,839
I've earned some money recently.

508
00:24:11,839 --> 00:24:13,759
Enough to cover your meals.

509
00:24:13,759 --> 00:24:15,800
Are you heading back later?

510
00:24:15,800 --> 00:24:16,920
Yes.

511
00:24:16,920 --> 00:24:18,400
I've got to get to Shunyi later.

512
00:24:18,400 --> 00:24:20,864
Still have repairs to do.

513
00:24:20,864 --> 00:24:22,320
Delivering goods,

514
00:24:22,320 --> 00:24:23,839
hauling ice,

515
00:24:23,839 --> 00:24:25,474
and now fixing things...

516
00:24:25,474 --> 00:24:27,725
When will this kind of life come to an end?

517
00:24:27,725 --> 00:24:30,361
School starts on the 16th of the first month.

518
00:24:33,440 --> 00:24:35,359
After the Lantern Festival.

519
00:24:35,359 --> 00:24:36,880
Don't worry.

520
00:24:36,880 --> 00:24:38,680
I'll come back.

521
00:24:39,594 --> 00:24:41,280
It's a deal.

522
00:24:42,469 --> 00:24:44,040
Deal.

523
00:24:46,833 --> 00:24:48,720
Xing Wu.

524
00:24:48,720 --> 00:24:50,640
You've been working so hard.

525
00:25:04,319 --> 00:25:05,360
Let's go.

526
00:25:05,360 --> 00:25:07,480
Or we'll really miss the bus.

527
00:25:08,182 --> 00:25:09,200
Okay.

528
00:25:09,200 --> 00:25:11,600
I'll try to walk faster.

529
00:25:27,119 --> 00:25:29,160
Why are you washing your hair here?

530
00:25:30,599 --> 00:25:33,240
The hot water ran out halfway through.

531
00:25:33,240 --> 00:25:35,720
So I'm just rinsing it off here.

532
00:25:37,059 --> 00:25:39,560
Don't catch a cold. Let me dry your hair.

533
00:27:15,400 --> 00:27:17,600
- Qing Ye, I'm coming in.
- Okay.

534
00:27:18,440 --> 00:27:20,040
Auntie.

535
00:27:22,680 --> 00:27:23,960
Classes start in two days.

536
00:27:23,960 --> 00:27:25,559
Mr. Zhu brought your uniforms.

537
00:27:25,559 --> 00:27:26,560
Two sets.

538
00:27:26,560 --> 00:27:28,686
I totally forgot about that.

539
00:27:29,519 --> 00:27:32,001
- It's a good fit.
- Good.

540
00:27:32,001 --> 00:27:33,299
It's the 15th tomorrow.

541
00:27:33,299 --> 00:27:35,519
What do you want to eat? I'll cook it for you.

542
00:27:35,519 --> 00:27:37,440
I like everything you cook, Auntie.

543
00:27:37,440 --> 00:27:40,119
You're such a sweet talker.

544
00:27:40,119 --> 00:27:41,575
I'll leave you to it.

545
00:28:44,799 --> 00:28:46,469
This is it.

546
00:29:26,640 --> 00:29:29,720
That's pretty much the situation.

547
00:29:29,720 --> 00:29:32,440
Everything is back to normal now.

548
00:29:32,440 --> 00:29:34,319
That's great.

549
00:29:34,319 --> 00:29:35,880
Here, try some nuts.

550
00:29:35,880 --> 00:29:37,867
- Thank you so much.
- Have some fruit.

551
00:29:37,867 --> 00:29:39,600
- Have some fruit.
- Thank you.

552
00:29:39,600 --> 00:29:40,720
It's nothing.

553
00:29:40,720 --> 00:29:42,440
Brother, have some fruit.

554
00:29:42,440 --> 00:29:43,676
And some nuts.

555
00:29:43,676 --> 00:29:45,280
It's delicious.

556
00:29:46,920 --> 00:29:48,721
I've heard that you've been

557
00:29:48,721 --> 00:29:50,881
taking good care of Ye.

558
00:29:52,559 --> 00:29:53,920
It's New Year's.

559
00:29:53,920 --> 00:29:56,160
I've prepared some gifts for all of you.

560
00:29:56,160 --> 00:29:58,480
Sun, hand them out.

561
00:29:59,150 --> 00:30:00,160
You didn't have to.

562
00:30:00,160 --> 00:30:01,359
Please take it.

563
00:30:01,359 --> 00:30:02,839
- No, no, no need.
- Just take it.

564
00:30:02,839 --> 00:30:04,160
- It's okay. Take it.
- No need.

565
00:30:04,160 --> 00:30:06,039
- Just take it.
- Okay, thanks.

566
00:30:06,039 --> 00:30:07,839
These are all top quality.

567
00:30:07,839 --> 00:30:08,960
I left in a hurry,

568
00:30:08,960 --> 00:30:10,039
so it's not much.

569
00:30:10,039 --> 00:30:11,920
I hope you don't mind.

570
00:30:11,920 --> 00:30:13,400
How could we?

571
00:30:13,400 --> 00:30:14,759
Don't worry.

572
00:30:14,759 --> 00:30:15,839
They're delighted.

573
00:30:15,839 --> 00:30:17,440
Yes, exactly.

574
00:30:17,440 --> 00:30:19,559
It's a long trip. You must be worn out.

575
00:30:19,559 --> 00:30:21,640
For lunch, we'll just have something simple.

576
00:30:21,640 --> 00:30:23,640
But tonight, we'll prepare

577
00:30:23,640 --> 00:30:26,079
some local dishes for you.

578
00:30:26,079 --> 00:30:27,320
Well then,

579
00:30:27,320 --> 00:30:29,559
Ye, just have a chat with your dad.

580
00:30:29,559 --> 00:30:31,880
We'll head out first. Let's go out.

581
00:30:31,880 --> 00:30:33,240
- Let's go.
- But these?

582
00:30:33,240 --> 00:30:34,519
Just take them.

583
00:30:34,519 --> 00:30:36,720
- Thank you.
- Thanks.

584
00:30:45,720 --> 00:30:47,039
Here, some tomatoes.

585
00:30:47,039 --> 00:30:48,560
Okay.

586
00:30:49,960 --> 00:30:52,667
What are those glass beads you're wearing?

587
00:30:52,667 --> 00:30:53,701
What?

588
00:30:53,701 --> 00:30:55,400
A big boss like him has seen expensive stuff.

589
00:30:55,400 --> 00:30:57,880
Why wear that heavy thing on your neck?

590
00:30:57,880 --> 00:30:59,480
Take it off quickly.

591
00:30:59,480 --> 00:31:00,519
- Take it off.
- But...

592
00:31:00,519 --> 00:31:03,519
- Keep a low profile.
- What are you doing?

593
00:31:03,519 --> 00:31:05,079
What are you doing? You...

594
00:31:05,079 --> 00:31:07,280
You even tucked it inside my collar.

595
00:31:07,960 --> 00:31:10,120
Leave a little bit out, okay?

596
00:31:11,824 --> 00:31:12,839
Seriously.

597
00:31:12,839 --> 00:31:14,680
Even though he's from the city,

598
00:31:14,680 --> 00:31:16,480
but his whole vibe

599
00:31:16,480 --> 00:31:18,519
is pretty much like my husband's.

600
00:31:18,519 --> 00:31:19,559
Come on.

601
00:31:19,559 --> 00:31:20,920
He smells really nice.

602
00:31:20,920 --> 00:31:21,961
He's got perfume on.

603
00:31:21,961 --> 00:31:24,439
Would your husband do that?

604
00:31:24,439 --> 00:31:26,000
Now that your brother-in-law is here,

605
00:31:26,000 --> 00:31:27,240
there's hope for Xuan Island

606
00:31:27,240 --> 00:31:29,672
to be rebuilt.

607
00:31:29,672 --> 00:31:30,960
That's for sure.

608
00:31:30,960 --> 00:31:32,519
Look at that car.

609
00:31:32,519 --> 00:31:33,759
It's worth more than 1,000,000 yuan.

610
00:31:33,759 --> 00:31:36,519
What kind of car costs 1,000,000 yuan?
Isn't that just a van?

611
00:31:36,519 --> 00:31:38,279
That's a luxury nanny van.

612
00:31:38,279 --> 00:31:40,520
A car for nannies?

613
00:31:41,359 --> 00:31:42,519
I can't talk to you.

614
00:31:42,519 --> 00:31:45,520
I don't care about all that.

615
00:31:46,319 --> 00:31:47,880
Anyway, I feel like I haven't

616
00:31:47,880 --> 00:31:49,920
taken good care of Ye.

617
00:31:49,920 --> 00:31:51,319
Now that her father is here,

618
00:31:51,319 --> 00:31:55,000
I'm afraid he'll want to
take her back immediately.

619
00:31:55,000 --> 00:31:57,119
After all, she's his own daughter.

620
00:31:57,119 --> 00:31:59,013
He came all this way.

621
00:31:59,013 --> 00:32:00,880
What else would it be for?

622
00:32:08,599 --> 00:32:10,188
Step back a bit.

623
00:32:10,188 --> 00:32:11,200
This way.

624
00:32:11,200 --> 00:32:12,680
Get the car logo in the shot.

625
00:32:12,680 --> 00:32:14,640
Don't make it too obvious.

626
00:32:14,640 --> 00:32:15,960
Do I look like

627
00:32:15,960 --> 00:32:17,839
I've driven 30,000 kilometers?

628
00:32:17,839 --> 00:32:19,920
Move over a bit.

629
00:32:19,920 --> 00:32:21,960
You're blocking the logo.

630
00:32:29,279 --> 00:32:31,400
- Hello, Uncle.
- Hello, Uncle.

631
00:32:34,839 --> 00:32:36,680
He's ignoring me.

632
00:32:36,680 --> 00:32:37,867
Cousin,

633
00:32:37,867 --> 00:32:40,319
your dad's car is awesome.

634
00:32:40,319 --> 00:32:41,640
It's nothing special.

635
00:32:41,640 --> 00:32:43,720
I hope we can get a chance

636
00:32:43,720 --> 00:32:45,520
to ride in it sometime.

637
00:32:47,119 --> 00:32:48,279
Ye,

638
00:32:48,279 --> 00:32:49,760
get in the car.

639
00:32:51,316 --> 00:32:52,360
- Hurry, hurry.
- I'm off.

640
00:32:52,360 --> 00:32:54,360
Okay. Bye.

641
00:32:58,160 --> 00:32:59,193
Goodbye, Uncle.

642
00:32:59,193 --> 00:33:00,800
Goodbye, Uncle.

643
00:33:02,656 --> 00:33:04,200
Where'd she go?

644
00:33:07,519 --> 00:33:09,880
- That scared me.
- He's driving pretty fast.

645
00:33:20,759 --> 00:33:23,365
I didn't expect that in such a short time,

646
00:33:23,365 --> 00:33:25,966
you'd be able to adapt to life here.

647
00:33:30,640 --> 00:33:33,440
People here are different from city folks.

648
00:33:33,440 --> 00:33:35,799
They're all very kind

649
00:33:35,799 --> 00:33:37,359
and sincere.

650
00:33:37,359 --> 00:33:40,161
When you get to know them, you'll find

651
00:33:40,161 --> 00:33:42,881
that these traits are precious.

652
00:33:47,119 --> 00:33:48,680
When I sent you here,

653
00:33:48,680 --> 00:33:50,839
I didn't have any other choice.

654
00:33:50,839 --> 00:33:53,079
Now everything is sorted out.

655
00:33:53,079 --> 00:33:54,760
I've already contacted the school.

656
00:33:54,760 --> 00:33:56,483
You can leave anytime.

657
00:33:56,483 --> 00:33:58,720
Haven't you always wanted to study abroad?

658
00:33:58,720 --> 00:34:01,319
But what if I don't want to leave now?

659
00:34:01,319 --> 00:34:03,519
Don't worry about the money.

660
00:34:03,519 --> 00:34:05,440
It's not the money.

661
00:34:06,119 --> 00:34:07,839
Sun Hai told me

662
00:34:07,839 --> 00:34:10,120
that you really wanted to leave Zhazhating.

663
00:34:13,159 --> 00:34:15,320
That was in the past.

664
00:34:17,239 --> 00:34:19,960
After I came here, I finally understood

665
00:34:20,879 --> 00:34:23,920
who really treats you well

666
00:34:23,920 --> 00:34:26,160
and who's just taking advantage of you.

667
00:34:27,000 --> 00:34:29,120
Who is a true friend...

668
00:34:30,360 --> 00:34:32,280
and who is just pretending.

669
00:34:32,280 --> 00:34:34,239
Friend?

670
00:34:34,239 --> 00:34:36,719
I've heard about your cousin

671
00:34:36,719 --> 00:34:39,920
being even worse
than those so-called friends of yours.

672
00:34:39,920 --> 00:34:41,040
He dropped out

673
00:34:41,040 --> 00:34:42,199
and hung out on the streets.

674
00:34:42,199 --> 00:34:43,960
Xing Wu is not like that.

675
00:34:43,960 --> 00:34:45,427
Don't judge someone

676
00:34:45,427 --> 00:34:47,326
just by what you've heard.

677
00:34:48,299 --> 00:34:51,239
During this time, I've realized one thing.

678
00:34:51,239 --> 00:34:52,440
Don't lower your standards.

679
00:34:52,440 --> 00:34:54,519
After you got into trouble,

680
00:34:54,519 --> 00:34:55,719
all those friends of yours

681
00:34:55,719 --> 00:34:57,800
stayed far away.

682
00:34:57,800 --> 00:34:58,969
You have no idea

683
00:34:58,969 --> 00:35:01,119
what I've been going through lately.

684
00:35:01,119 --> 00:35:03,000
When I hit rock bottom,

685
00:35:03,000 --> 00:35:06,000
it was the people in Zhazhating
who reached out to help me.

686
00:35:06,000 --> 00:35:07,400
They taught me a lot.

687
00:35:07,400 --> 00:35:08,920
Enough.

688
00:35:08,920 --> 00:35:11,000
I'm done talking about this.

689
00:35:12,239 --> 00:35:13,880
Anyway, you have no say

690
00:35:13,880 --> 00:35:15,360
in going back to Beijing.

691
00:35:15,360 --> 00:35:16,559
Pack up your things.

692
00:35:16,559 --> 00:35:18,320
You're coming home with me tomorrow.

693
00:35:18,320 --> 00:35:19,721
You haven't even asked what I want

694
00:35:19,721 --> 00:35:22,039
before making choices for me.

695
00:35:22,039 --> 00:35:23,079
Ye.

696
00:35:23,079 --> 00:35:24,280
The moment Mr. Qing was out,

697
00:35:24,280 --> 00:35:25,519
he arranged everything

698
00:35:25,519 --> 00:35:26,760
and came straight to Zhazhating.

699
00:35:26,760 --> 00:35:28,199
He just cares about you.

700
00:35:28,199 --> 00:35:29,400
He wants to be with you

701
00:35:29,400 --> 00:35:31,199
and take you home as soon as possible.

702
00:35:31,199 --> 00:35:32,560
Cares about me? He's just

703
00:35:32,560 --> 00:35:34,880
making decisions for me in his way.

704
00:35:34,880 --> 00:35:36,000
You did it then,

705
00:35:36,000 --> 00:35:37,280
and you're doing it again.

706
00:35:37,280 --> 00:35:39,880
Have you ever thought about my feelings?

707
00:35:40,920 --> 00:35:43,199
The only reason I didn't take you today

708
00:35:43,199 --> 00:35:45,240
is that I respect your feelings.

709
00:35:45,864 --> 00:35:48,360
Still time to say goodbye to your friends.

710
00:35:51,199 --> 00:35:53,159
How considerate of you.

711
00:35:53,159 --> 00:35:54,559
And what if I don't want to leave?

712
00:35:54,559 --> 00:35:56,679
You have no choice.

713
00:35:56,679 --> 00:35:58,280
The way you're acting right now

714
00:35:58,280 --> 00:36:01,487
is exactly why I can't allow you
to stay here any longer.

715
00:36:02,372 --> 00:36:03,400
Your mother and I worked

716
00:36:03,400 --> 00:36:04,440
so hard to raise you.

717
00:36:04,440 --> 00:36:06,960
How can I just let you
throw yourself away in a place like this?

718
00:36:06,960 --> 00:36:09,000
Don't bring Mom into this.

719
00:36:14,519 --> 00:36:15,960
Fine.

720
00:36:17,519 --> 00:36:19,000
If we can't even talk this through,

721
00:36:19,000 --> 00:36:21,840
let's not waste our time.

722
00:36:23,000 --> 00:36:24,599
I'll pick you up at 7:00 a.m. tomorrow.

723
00:36:24,599 --> 00:36:26,000
Sun.

724
00:37:14,055 --> 00:37:15,080
<i>We did it.</i>

725
00:37:15,080 --> 00:37:17,484
<i>- Is it done? Grandma, do I look good?
- Absolutely!</i>

726
00:37:17,484 --> 00:37:20,916
<i>Looks great! Looks great!</i>

727
00:37:46,079 --> 00:37:48,119
<i>It... it tastes pretty good.</i>

728
00:37:48,119 --> 00:37:50,360
<i>Good, isn't it? I said it was good.</i>

729
00:37:50,360 --> 00:37:53,680
<i>Give Ye another bowl.</i>

730
00:38:16,679 --> 00:38:17,928
<i>Tell me,</i>

731
00:38:17,928 --> 00:38:20,719
<i>what on earth did you put in here?</i>

732
00:38:20,719 --> 00:38:23,480
<i>This is way too heavy.</i>

733
00:38:24,519 --> 00:38:26,719
<i>What's that smell? It's so strong.</i>

734
00:38:26,719 --> 00:38:28,720
<i>You've never used a mosquito coil before?</i>

735
00:38:29,853 --> 00:38:31,679
<i>Just a friendly reminder.</i>

736
00:38:31,679 --> 00:38:32,920
<i>These mosquitoes are nasty enough</i>

737
00:38:32,920 --> 00:38:34,320
<i>to kill a pig.</i>

738
00:38:34,320 --> 00:38:35,466
<i>How many bites you got?</i>

739
00:38:35,466 --> 00:38:37,119
<i>Who are you calling a pig?</i>

740
00:38:37,119 --> 00:38:39,125
<i>Are you installing an air conditioner for me?</i>

741
00:38:39,125 --> 00:38:40,510
<i>A second-hand unit from the shop.</i>

742
00:38:40,510 --> 00:38:42,440
<i>Just use it for now.</i>

743
00:38:42,440 --> 00:38:44,320
<i>This isn't just a second-hand air conditioner.</i>

744
00:38:44,320 --> 00:38:47,440
<i>This is a leap in my living standards!</i>

745
00:38:52,119 --> 00:38:53,440
<i>This one,</i>

746
00:38:53,440 --> 00:38:54,719
<i>the thinnest and smallest one,</i>

747
00:38:54,719 --> 00:38:56,079
<i>is Yao Ji.</i>

748
00:38:56,079 --> 00:38:57,280
<i>This one is Bai Ban.</i>

749
00:38:57,280 --> 00:38:59,360
<i>And that one is Fa Cai.</i>

750
00:38:59,360 --> 00:39:01,159
<i>Don't tell me you're the one</i>

751
00:39:01,159 --> 00:39:02,519
<i>who got my computer back?</i>

752
00:39:02,519 --> 00:39:04,079
<i>If you'd like to think so,</i>

753
00:39:04,079 --> 00:39:05,800
<i>then yes, it was me.</i>

754
00:39:05,800 --> 00:39:07,119
<i>What,</i>

755
00:39:07,119 --> 00:39:09,120
<i>you're going to bow down to me three times?</i>

756
00:39:21,440 --> 00:39:22,519
<i>Look.</i>

757
00:39:22,519 --> 00:39:23,760
<i>Even a paper plane</i>

758
00:39:23,760 --> 00:39:26,360
<i>can find a different way to fly.</i>

759
00:39:26,360 --> 00:39:29,160
<i>Do you really not want to change your mind?</i>

760
00:39:38,840 --> 00:39:40,840
<i>You're beautiful!</i>

761
00:39:40,840 --> 00:39:42,559
<i>Beautiful, beautiful.</i>

762
00:39:42,559 --> 00:39:44,720
<i>- Pretty nice, right?
- I think you look even better</i>

763
00:39:44,720 --> 00:39:46,360
<i>than the models on TV.</i>

764
00:39:46,360 --> 00:39:48,200
<i>Really.</i>

765
00:40:04,598 --> 00:40:06,280
- Ye.
- Uncle Sun.

766
00:40:06,280 --> 00:40:08,280
This is a down jacket your dad bought for you.

767
00:40:08,280 --> 00:40:10,400
It's cold. Put it on.

768
00:40:16,913 --> 00:40:19,078
Sorry if I'm out of line.

769
00:40:19,078 --> 00:40:20,800
I have children too.

770
00:40:20,800 --> 00:40:22,480
What father could bear to see

771
00:40:22,480 --> 00:40:25,360
his daughter go without a decent
down jacket in the bitter cold?

772
00:40:25,360 --> 00:40:26,400
On that point,

773
00:40:26,400 --> 00:40:28,840
I can understand how your dad feels.

774
00:40:29,552 --> 00:40:30,880
Uncle Sun,

775
00:40:30,880 --> 00:40:33,120
you don't have to speak for him.

776
00:40:33,719 --> 00:40:35,640
Since you call me Uncle Sun,

777
00:40:35,640 --> 00:40:37,719
I'll tell you what's on my mind.

778
00:40:37,719 --> 00:40:38,800
I can tell

779
00:40:38,800 --> 00:40:40,239
that your auntie's family

780
00:40:40,239 --> 00:40:41,840
has indeed been very good to you.

781
00:40:41,840 --> 00:40:42,960
After all this time,

782
00:40:42,960 --> 00:40:44,760
you've grown attached to them.

783
00:40:44,760 --> 00:40:46,519
At their most difficult moment,

784
00:40:46,519 --> 00:40:47,928
you don't want to leave them behind.

785
00:40:47,928 --> 00:40:50,817
I hear you on that.

786
00:40:51,800 --> 00:40:53,120
But Ye,

787
00:40:53,120 --> 00:40:54,602
look.

788
00:40:54,602 --> 00:40:56,000
Your auntie's family

789
00:40:56,000 --> 00:40:57,679
just barely survived a disaster.

790
00:40:57,679 --> 00:40:59,440
Their boat's got holes everywhere.

791
00:40:59,440 --> 00:41:00,960
Four people on it,

792
00:41:00,960 --> 00:41:02,880
and you'll never keep up with the water.

793
00:41:02,880 --> 00:41:04,360
It's going down.

794
00:41:04,360 --> 00:41:06,719
If someone gets off early,

795
00:41:06,719 --> 00:41:09,197
it'll be better for everyone.

796
00:41:10,960 --> 00:41:12,519
If you split one pancake into four pieces,

797
00:41:12,519 --> 00:41:13,920
no one gets enough to eat.

798
00:41:13,920 --> 00:41:15,400
If you leave now,

799
00:41:15,400 --> 00:41:17,239
it's not only for your dad,

800
00:41:17,239 --> 00:41:19,160
it's also to help them.

801
00:41:28,360 --> 00:41:30,240
Ye, you're back.

802
00:41:30,920 --> 00:41:32,840
Why did you come back alone?

803
00:41:32,840 --> 00:41:34,560
Where's your dad?

804
00:41:36,519 --> 00:41:38,679
What's wrong?

805
00:41:38,679 --> 00:41:40,960
Did you two fight?

806
00:41:40,960 --> 00:41:42,519
Auntie,

807
00:41:42,519 --> 00:41:44,440
my dad wants to bring me home.

808
00:41:51,960 --> 00:41:53,000
I expected that.

809
00:41:53,000 --> 00:41:54,440
That's normal.

810
00:41:54,440 --> 00:41:56,320
It's a good thing.

811
00:41:57,280 --> 00:41:58,880
Did your dad say when you're leaving?

812
00:41:58,880 --> 00:42:00,200
If your dad's not in a rush,

813
00:42:00,200 --> 00:42:02,800
you can go after tomorrow's Lantern Festival.

814
00:42:02,800 --> 00:42:04,800
That way, you can spend a few more days here.

815
00:42:04,800 --> 00:42:06,000
You can show your dad around

816
00:42:06,000 --> 00:42:07,920
and let him see the place.

817
00:42:07,920 --> 00:42:10,840
Just stay as long as possible.

818
00:42:10,840 --> 00:42:12,840
We're leaving tomorrow morning.

819
00:42:33,960 --> 00:42:35,360
<i>Wu,</i>

820
00:42:35,360 --> 00:42:37,119
<i>Qing Ye's dad is here to take her home.</i>

821
00:42:37,119 --> 00:42:38,893
<i>They're leaving tomorrow morning.</i>

822
00:42:47,439 --> 00:42:48,559
Xing Wu.

823
